From: Plain Browser
Subject: [crash] Crashpad uploads to crash.plain-browser.app when the user turned crash reports on

Category: 95-crash. ungoogled's disable-crash-reporter.patch (dropped in upstream-revert.list) switches Crashpad
off on Windows; with it back, dumps are written locally (chrome://crashes) as in Chromium. Uploading needs two
things Chromium ties to Google Chrome and metrics:
- the URL: ChromeCrashReporterClient::GetUploadUrl() returns plainbrowser::crash::kUploadUrl (a Cloudflare
  Worker, infra/crash-reports); the base class returns one only for Google Chrome builds;
- the consent: ChromeCrashReporterClient::GetCollectStatsConsent() reads our registry value
  (HKCU\<install_static::GetRegistryPath()>\PlainBrowserCrashReports = 1) instead of the metrics "usagestats"
  value; the MetricsReportingEnabled policy still wins. ChromeMetricsServicesManagerClient::UpdateRunningServices
  no longer passes the metrics state to Crashpad, which would switch uploads off whenever metrics are off (always,
  in Plain Browser).
The Local State pref plainbrowser.crash_reports.enabled (default off, Settings > Privacy and security, 60-ui/0012)
is registered in RegisterLocalState; StartCrashConsent (PostBrowserStart, after the filter list updater of
30-adblock/0006) mirrors it into that registry value and the running Crashpad. Code: //plainbrowser/crash.
